From 27fdca64c14a7704b2bb284b3c1ed071947b5949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:08:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the staged temp.dict goes after the dictionary loops,
 not before them

gendict.pl leaves a 3-byte temp.dict in the source www (ASUS gitignores it); on a
warm tree the `for F in $(wildcard *.dict)` loops stage it as an empty 26th
dictionary and reaper_verify's i18n-dict check sees line counts 0 and 8832. The
rule's existing rm runs before the loops; this one runs after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b2df5e9d90546367653c4875c60453e7f43fbc66)
---
 release/src/router/www/Makefile | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Makefile b/release/src/router/www/Makefile
index 670d1f0b737..df440627908 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Makefile
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Makefile
@@ -397,6 +397,10 @@ else
 		./gendict.pl $(BUILD_NAME) $$F $(INSTALLDIR)/www/$$F; \
 	done
 endif
+	# reaper 2026-10-27: gendict.pl leaves a 3-byte temp.dict in the source www (gitignored), so on a warm tree
+	# the wildcard loops above stage it as an empty 26th dictionary. Not a dictionary - drop the staged copy here,
+	# after the loops (the rm near the top of this rule runs before they do).
+	rm -f $(INSTALLDIR)/www/temp.dict
 	# reaper 2026-10-25 (review 2026-10-24, Q-C2-10): /* */ and // comments out of Reaper's own pages, scripts and
 	# stylesheets - the vendor minifier above leaves them (its strip_comments() is a stub). A file the stripper cannot
 	# lex is left as it is, and the build never fails on it (build-scripts/tests/test_reaper_strip.py proves the tokens).
-- 
